course: dictionary
lesson: 11050
title: Old words, formal words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to old books, history and official papers. Wedlock is one of them. You will rarely hear it at home or at school, but you may meet it in a history book or an old story. Wedlock means the state of being married.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Born out of wedlock» is a set phrase. The words out of show the child was outside wedlock, so the parents were not married. The word born tells you the phrase is about a baby and its parents.
explain: Today people say marriage or being married instead. If you meet wedlock, swap in marriage and check the sentence still makes sense. The meaning is nearly the same, but wedlock sounds older and more formal.
fact: Wedlock is a noun, and it has no plural.
fact: Wedlock means the state of being married.
fact: Wedlock is formal and old-fashioned, so you will find it in old books, history and legal language.
fact: «Born out of wedlock» means born to parents who were not married.
fact: In everyday speech, people say marriage or being married instead.
exercise: «Her grandparents lived in wedlock for fifty years.» What does wedlock mean here? | Living in a big house | *Being married | Working together on a farm | Owning a shop
exercise: Which everyday word means the same as wedlock? | Lock | Holiday | Birthday | *Marriage
exercise: «The old diary said the boy was born out of wedlock.» What does this tell you? | *His parents were not married | He was born in the spring | His parents were married in a church | He was born on a boat
test: What does wedlock mean? | A kind of bread | A long walk in the woods | A type of door lock | *The state of being married
test: Which phrase is an old, formal way of saying a child was born to parents who were not married? | Born on a farm | *Born out of wedlock | Born with a smile | Born in the spring
exam: Which everyday word best replaces wedlock in «Their wedlock lasted sixty years.»? | Holiday | Football | *Marriage | Breakfast
